   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 3^{x}\\,e^{\\sin(3x)} \\). Find the value of \\( f'(0) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Ln",
            3
         ],
         3
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 3^{x} \\) and \\( e^{\\sin(3x)} \\), so the product rule comes first: \\( f'(x) = \\left(3^{x}\\right)'\\,e^{\\sin(3x)} + 3^{x}\\left(e^{\\sin(3x)}\\right)' \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               3,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Sin",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     3,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 3^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               3,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( e^{\\sin(3x)} \\) is an exponential of \\( \\sin(3x) \\), which is a sine of \\( 3x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(e^{\\sin(3x)}\\right)' = 3 e^{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Sin",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     3,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Cos",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  3,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Assemble the product rule and evaluate at \\( x = 0 \\): \\( f'(0) = \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} + 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Ln",
               3
            ],
            3
         ]
      }
   ],
